From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Subject: [PATCH] luma: every application window gets Luma's corners

GTK and libadwaita windows round their own corners; Electron, Chromium,
Qt and undecorated X11 windows draw a plain rectangle, so Discord, Claude
and ChatGPT sat on the desktop with sharp corners beside rounded windows.
The compositor now masks every window that is not a GTK application to the
toolkit's 15px radius, on its frame, so a client's own shadow is left as it
is. Mutter-framed X11 windows, fullscreen windows and Android windows are
left as they are.

